          deepDive: "**ゆえ（故）** is a classical noun meaning *reason, cause*, and **〜がゆえ(に)** means *because of ~, precisely because ~* — a formal, literary alternative to から／ので／ため, as the book says. It often implies that the result follows **from the very nature** of the cause: 愛するがゆえに、子どもに厳しくする (*precisely because they love them, parents are strict*); 文字として読めないがゆえに、空間の美を純粋に鑑賞できる (*precisely because they can't be read as characters, we can appreciate the beauty of the space*).\n\nConnection (が is the classical particle, not the subject marker):\n- **Plain form + がゆえ(に)**: 読めないがゆえに, 美しいがゆえに, 不十分であったがゆえに.\n- **なA／N + である + がゆえ(に)**: 静かであるがゆえに, 学生であるがゆえに. ✗学生だがゆえに is wrong.\n- **なA + な + ゆえ, N (の) + ゆえ** (the ＊ note): 不慣れなゆえに (*because one is new to it*), 若さゆえの過ち (*mistakes of youth*).\n- **〜がゆえの + N**: 愛するがゆえの厳しさ (*strictness born of love*).\n- **ゆえに／それゆえ(に)** as a conjunction, *therefore*: a＝b、b＝c。ゆえにa＝c.\n\nRegister: formal and written (essays, editorials, speeches, logic and mathematics). In conversation it sounds deliberately stiff or dramatic.\n\nCompare:\n- **〜ため(に)**: neutral written cause: 雨のため中止 (*canceled due to rain*); ゆえ would sound overblown here.\n- **〜からこそ**: *precisely because*, the everyday way to add the same emphasis: 愛しているからこそ厳しくする.\n- **〜こととて** (#68): old-fashioned *since (it is ~)*, usually excusing oneself: 慣れないこととて (*as I'm not used to it*). がゆえ has no apologetic tone.\n- **〜とあって** (#2): *because of this special circumstance*, with a natural visible result (crowds, popularity).\n- **NがN（な）だけに** (#53): *given what kind of N it is*: 業種が業種なだけに (*given the type of business*).\n\nCommon mistake: ✗子どもだがゆえに → ✓子どもであるがゆえに / 子どもゆえに.\n\nJLPT tip: がゆえに is the reason option in 問題1: 独創性を重んじるがゆえに、伝統を古臭いと否定する (*because originality is prized, tradition is dismissed as old-fashioned*). Rule out the contrastive とはいえ／どころか and おかげで (credit for a good result). Check the connection: N and なA need である, or drop the が.",
