          deepDive: "**禁じる** *to forbid, to hold back* + **得ない（えない）** *cannot*: **N + を禁じえない** = literally *cannot hold back N*, i.e. **cannot suppress N, cannot help feeling N**. The book: feeling an emotion so strongly that one cannot keep it in. 疑問を禁じえない (*I cannot suppress my doubts*).\n\nConnection: N + を禁じえない (kanji: 禁じ得ない; polite: 禁じえません). N is a **feeling** or its outward sign (the ＊ note: 怒り・悲しみ・同情・とまどい): 驚き, 憤り, 失望, 疑問, 感動, 惜別の念, 涙.\n\nNuance: the emotion rises irresistibly from something external that the writer sees or learns. Typical frame: [situation] + とは／に + N を禁じえない: この絵が1億円もするとは、驚きを禁じえない (*I can't help being astonished that this picture costs 100 million yen*); 人々の姿に涙を禁じえなかった (*I couldn't hold back my tears at the sight of them*).\n\nRegister: very formal and written (editorials, reviews, formal speeches, farewells): 教授のご退官にあたり、惜別の念を禁じえません (*on the professor's retirement, we cannot hold back our sorrow at parting*). In conversation: 驚かずにはいられない, 思わず泣いてしまった.\n\nSubject: the speaker (or a group including the speaker). For someone else, hedge it: 彼は失望を禁じえなかったようだ (*he apparently couldn't hide his disappointment*).\n\nCompare:\n- **〜ずにはいられない**: *can't help ~ing*, the everyday equivalent, after verbs: 同情せずにはいられない (*I can't help feeling sorry*).\n- **〜にたえない** (#69): *overwhelmed with*, formal, mostly with 感謝・喜び・遺憾 in speeches: 感謝の念にたえません (*I am deeply grateful*).\n- **〜てやまない** (#15): a lasting, heartfelt wish: ご成功を願ってやみません (*I sincerely wish you success*).\n- **〜を余儀なくされる** (#9): *be forced to ~*: 中止を余儀なくされた (*had no choice but to cancel*). The same を + stiff verb shape, but about actions forced by circumstances, not feelings.\n\nCommon mistakes: ✗行くことを禁じえない (only feelings); ✗驚きが禁じえない → ✓驚きを禁じえない (the particle is を).\n\nJLPT tip: feeling noun + を + blank → 禁じえない. In ordering questions the chain is [cause] + に + [feeling] + を禁じえない: 名優の素晴らしい演技に感動を禁じえない (*can't help being moved by the great actor's wonderful performance*).",
